From 52696394415d7e5f1193c80b5ee51f0be57af3ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:11:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: publish WebTransport discovery and rotating browser
 certificates

Add opt-in overlapping ten-day browser leaves using the unchanged EC P-256
node TLS key. Recover current/next hashes across restart, promote the
previous successor before replacing it, and reload by generation before a
new inbound TLS session. Keep existing contexts alive across rollover and
preserve published-leaf metadata after a successor-write failure.

Extend getwebtransportinfo and serve GET/HEAD /p2p/wt/info on the bounded
HTTP worker queue. Public discovery omits tokens and private connection,
fallback and cache counters. Keep generic HTTP resources free of blanket
H3 Alt-Svc because the QUIC listener supports WT P2P only. Document actual
Origin, identity, proxy and browser trust constraints; retain p2p-v1.

Replace the obsolete echo-CLI browser harness with bounded actual-node
checks using fresh owned data/profiles, strict protocol/close results and
no global trust or certificate-error bypass. Native daemon 43/unit 171
builds, 37 cases/13630 assertions, rotation/live-leaf, existing fallback
and HTTP metrics checks pass. Actual Chrome 155 hash mode passes. Stock
local-CA mode rejects; explicit development-CA controls reject untrusted
and accept profile-trusted roots while preserving chain/hostname checks.
This is not stock public-CA or reverse-proxy acceptance. Preserve failed
stock runs and partial raw NetLogs; no broad sweep or benchmark ran.
W10-W12 and the external interoperability gates remain outstanding.

Coordinator ordered integration (2026-10-20):
Existing causal fixes and mechanical namespace/format adaptations are folded at their first responsible owner. Exact inputs and prefix adaptations are recorded in integration-next final delivery; original author provenance is retained.
